// Syncthing allowlist for the private ml/output/ tree and the gitignored CLAUDE.md.
//
// Code travels via git; only the private outputs (annotation, splits,
// checkpoints, production, training, evaluation) and CLAUDE.md travel via Syncthing.
// Syncing .git/ across machines corrupts repos, and the venv (7.7G) is
// machine-specific -- so this file inverts the usual default: it admits
// ml/output/ and ignores everything else.
//
// ORDERING IS LOAD-BEARING. Syncthing matches top-down, first match wins, and
// silently expands a bare directory pattern to cover its children too: `!/ml`
// also means `!/ml/**`. So a broad un-ignore placed too early re-admits the
// whole tree. Each level therefore goes: admit the payload, ignore the other
// children, THEN un-ignore the directory itself so Syncthing descends into it.
// Verify any edit with: GET /rest/db/ignores?folder=<id> and re-check
// localBytes on /rest/db/status -- it should be ~3.2G (all of ml/output/).

// -- root CLAUDE.md: gitignored, so Syncthing is the only way it travels --
!/CLAUDE.md

// -- ml: admit ml/output, ignore the other children (.venv, data, source), then allow the dir --
!/ml/output
/ml/*
!/ml

// -- everything else in the repo, .git included --
*
